Things to clean up

Server / Conn

2. One subscriber's failed send closes the publisher (Broker.handlePublish)
   - try sess.sendMsg(pub_packet) bubbles a subscriber's error up through
     handlePacket, so Server closes the publisher, whose packet was fine.
   - The error belongs to the subscriber's conn.

3. Small stuff
   - The parse error log in handleConnEv prints clientId, which is empty
     before CONNECT. Print the fd like the read error does.
   - handleSocketEv takes ev and never uses it.
   - Server.ip and Server.port are stored but never read.
   - Conn.clean_session is set in handleConnect but never read. Session has
     its own.
   - Server.deinit doesn't free the open conns.

Broker / Session

4. conns key dangles after a takeover (Broker.appendConn)
   - fetchPut only replaces the value when the key exists. The key stays a
     slice of the old Conn's client_id_buf, which is freed when the old conn
     closes. Later lookups compare against freed memory.

5. removeSession leaks the session's messages (Broker.removeSession)
   - Destroys the Session without freeing queued_msgs (the deque and the
     duped topic/payload) or the inflight msgs. Happens when a clean=1
     connect discards a clean=0 session that had queued messages.

6. Resume doesn't resend inflight messages (Broker.handleConnect)
   - On reconnect with clean_session=0 the server MUST resend unacked QoS 1/2
     PUBLISH packets with DUP=1 and their original packet IDs, plus pending
     PUBREL [MQTT-4.4.0-1]. Only queued_msgs get drained.

7. drainQueuedMsgs drops messages on a failed send (Session.drainQueuedMsgs)
   - catch continue skips the msg, and its topic/payload are never freed.

8. appendInflightMsg overwrites the oldest message when full
   (Session.appendInflightMsg)
   - The overwritten msg's topic/payload leak, and a QoS 1/2 message is lost
     before it was acked.

9. Inflight msgs mix owned and borrowed slices (Session.appendInflightMsg)
   - sendPublish stores the caller's msg as-is, while drainQueuedMsgs moves
     duped queue msgs in. Nothing can tell which topic/payload to free.

Session tests

10. "inflight buffer is full" uses a length that can't happen
    - inflight_msgs_len = max_inflight_msgs + 1, but the length never goes
      past max_inflight_msgs. The test passes with >= or >, so an off-by-one
      slips through. Use max_inflight_msgs and check inflight_msgs_len didn't
      change.

11. page_allocator hides leaks
    - appendQueuedMsg dupes topic/payload and nothing frees them.
      std.testing.allocator would catch it, but Session has no deinit yet.

12. Empty topic/payload never exercise the dupe
    - With real bytes the test can check the queued copy has the same content
      in different memory.

13. "offline client" builds an invalid QoS 0 PUBLISH
    - dup = true, but DUP MUST be 0 for QoS 0 [MQTT-3.3.1-2].
    - QoS 0 has no packet id, so checking packet_id checks a field that's
      never sent. Check topic/payload instead.

14. "gets added to the inflight queue" only checks state (optional)
    - Reading fds[1] and checking the PUBLISH bytes would show the send works.

15. drainQueuedMsgs has no tests.
